# Policy the architecture leaves open on purpose — these come from bench
# measurement, not from a number picked in advance. See
# docs/firmware_architecture.md "Open items".
#
# Kept out of app/Kconfig so the test suites can source the same symbols the
# application builds with: a suite that hardcoded 600 ms would keep passing
# after someone changed the window.

config TK_SELECTOR_SETTLE_MS
    int "Selector settle window (ms)"
    default 600
    help
      A selector contact transition must be stable for this long before a deck
      change is published. Ignores make/break chatter and stops the panel from
      flashing through intermediate positions while the knob is turning.

config TK_NEXT_DEBOUNCE_MS
    int "Next button debounce (ms)"
    default 30
    help
      One physical press must produce exactly one event. Press duration has no
      meaning; long press is Next. The debounce itself is done by the in-tree
      gpio-keys driver, so this must match `debounce-interval-ms` in the board
      overlay — devicetree is processed before Kconfig and cannot read it.

config TK_FULL_REFRESH_INTERVAL
    int "Partial refreshes between full refreshes"
    default 8
    help
      Determine this from ghosting observed on the breadboard panel. A cold
      boot always uses a full refresh because the panel content is unknown.

config TK_PLAYBACK_DEPTH_MAX
    int "Maximum editorial depth in normal playback"
    default 2
    range 1 3
    help
      Depth 3 is never drawn automatically. Changing this away from 2 breaks
      the consent model in docs/design.md.

config TK_RECENT_RING
    int "Questions excluded from the start of a new bag cycle"
    default 20
    help
      Shared across all decks, so turning the selector cannot immediately
      return a question just seen under a different deck.

config TK_REFRESH_MIN_MV
    int "Minimum cell voltage for a panel refresh (mV)"
    default 3200
    help
      A partial refresh attempted near brownout can leave the panel in a
      corrupted state. Below this, the previous question stays on screen.
